From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(DisksMenu): only /home's partition, and the SD card on
 an internal install

The Disks settings menu listed udisks2's "unprotected" devices: every
disk but the one holding /home, each once per partition with no
filesystem, so a handheld's internal storage filled it with the vendor's
partitions (super, vbmeta, xbl, ...) and the disk RetroForge keeps its
data on was missing. It now reads the mount table (shown_disks.gd) and
shows the disk holding /home with that partition alone (on the internal
storage or on the SD card booted from), and, when /home is not on an SD
card, the SD card with its mounted partitions. The mount table is read
again each time the menu is shown, and each second while it is: an SD
card is mounted after udisks2 reports it, and again after a format,
with no udisks2 signal.

A partition card shows the partition's main mount point alone, the
first place its whole filesystem is mounted: udisks2 lists the bind
mounts too, and /home's partition is also bound at /opt, /root, /srv,
/var/cache/pacman, /var/log, ... (an SD card at /run/retroforge/sdcard). Its
size is the filesystem's free space of its size while it is mounted
("24.65 GB free of 24.73 GB", from df), the partition's size when not.
---
